irp|v|To fail in duty; to offend. ; To fail in fulfilling a contract, agreement, or duty. ; To fail to appear in court; to let a case go by default. ; To fail to perform or pay; to be guilty of neglect of; to omit; as, to default a dividend. ; To call a defendant or other party whose duty it is to be present in court, and make entry of his default, if he fails to appear; to enter a default against. ; To leave out of account; to omit.	o:26gu,16,2;1n68,8,1;1vf8,3,3~1vf8,3,3;26gu,16,2;1n68,8,1	d:1c3a,3,1~1c3a,3,1	D:f0n,44,4;1n68,8,1~f0n,44,4;1n68,8,1
