j4h|a|A tract of land shaped like the letter delta (/), especially when the land is alluvial and inclosed between two or more mouths of a river; as, the delta of the Ganges, of the Nile, or of the Mississippi.	j:1sb8,87,5;189d,51,4;1mx9,49,21;1899,41,9;1hju,35,2;225l,23,1;qif,10,3~1mx9,49,21;1899,41,9;1sb8,87,5;189d,51,4;qif,10,3;1hju,35,2;225l,23,1
