jg7|a|Hanging down; as, a dependent bough or leaf. ; Relying on, or subject to, something else for support; not able to exist, or sustain itself, or to perform anything, without the will, power, or aid of something else; not self-sustaining; contingent or conditioned; subordinate; -- often with on or upon; as, dependent on God; dependent upon friends.	j:28kz,50,1~28kz,50,1	e:xvq,67,4;yn2,67,15;2032,61,7;24ne,51,3;p73,47,3;ekj,36,3;2911,23,9;1byh,19,11;1poa,15,3;24gy,14,3;16ri,7,1;2eq,6,4~yn2,67,15;1byh,19,11;2911,23,9;2032,61,7;2eq,6,4;xvq,67,4;ekj,36,3;p73,47,3;24ne,51,3;24gy,14,3;1poa,15,3;16ri,7,1
